Z||000037||Bazooka||10-25-2001||06:24 PM||||I add a 'Torco' octane booster to each tankful of premium to bring it up to about 107 octane. I have about 12 to 1 compression (about 192 psi per cylinder compression). I also only get about 8-10 miles per gallon. Using the higher octane (slower burning fuel) does help pinging.||||reg||1
Z||000038||ray b||10-25-2001||06:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> You are incorrect. Premium is  NOT "less explosive". It's flash point is higher. This causes the air/fuel mixture to burn in an even pattern. When the air/fuel burns unevenly or self-ignites, you have pinging. <BR>As the fuel burns evenly and completely you have smoother performance and lower emissions. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>NO BTU ARE LESS AND MAKE LESS POWER. UNLESS IT KNOCKS [PRESPARK EXPLOSION]ONLY THEN DO YOU NEED HIGHER TEST.SMOOTHER YES MORE POWER NO.WASTE YOU $$$$ IF YOU WANT TO.LITE PING UNDER LOADS IS NORMAL AND NOT A BIG PROBLEM UNLIKE HARD KNOCKS THAT WILL DAMMAGE YOUR MOTOR QUICKLY BUT STOCK CLEAN FIERO'S DONOT NEED HI=TEST GAS 4 OR 6, HIGHER COMPRESSION MOTORS DO BUT NOT STOCK.<BR>ARAB'S AND OIL CO'S HAVE ENUFF $$$$ SAVE YOURS.<P><P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000039||88CoupeV6||10-25-2001||06:35 PM||||Only moble and only 89, I get 27 MPG on my 88GT. I've tried every brand and octane and that is the one that seems to be best for me. The 88CoupeV6 likes 93.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000040||Cooter||10-25-2001||08:52 PM||||My 3.4 hates the reg. fuel, will tolerate the middle grade but does best with the premium. Even with a knock sensor ecm system, it still will spark knock pretty bad with the cheap stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000041||Oreif||10-25-2001||09:10 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Originally posted by ray b:<BR>NO BTU ARE LESS AND MAKE LESS POWER. UNLESS IT KNOCKS [PRESPARK EXPLOSION]ONLY THEN DO YOU NEED HIGHER TEST.SMOOTHER YES MORE POWER NO.WASTE YOU $$$$ IF YOU WANT TO.LITE PING UNDER LOADS IS NORMAL AND NOT A BIG PROBLEM UNLIKE HARD KNOCKS THAT WILL DAMMAGE YOUR MOTOR QUICKLY BUT STOCK CLEAN FIERO'S DONOT NEED HI=TEST GAS 4 OR 6, HIGHER COMPRESSION MOTORS DO BUT NOT STOCK.<BR>ARAB'S AND OIL CO'S HAVE ENUFF $$$$ SAVE YOURS.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Again you have your facts incorrect. Below is the BTU's per Gallon for each Octane rating. This was taken from Exxon's website.<P>Gasoline 87 Octane Gallon 105,000  <BR>Gasoline 89 Octane Gallon 110,200  <BR>Gasoline 92 Octane Gallon 115,000  <P><BR>So Premium (92 Octane) has 15,000 more BTU's per gallon than 87 Octane.<BR>Higher Octane fuels burn faster, more even, and hotter than lower octane fuels. But the inital flash point under compression is higher thus reducing pinging. The faster and more even the burn in the cylinders the more power you will have.<P>Even light pinging can damage an engine over time.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000042||Tina||10-25-2001||09:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrtgman:<BR><B>How about racing fuel? Anyone ever try that in their fiero?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Don't know about racing fuel,but their is been times the truck to refuel the bosses <BR>helicopter was sitting right next to my Fiero at the shop Eric works at.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>But usually it's premium.<P>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
